@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+---
+id: dl-005-generate-deterministic-structural-json-patch-diffs
+type: decision-log
+title: "Generate deterministic structural JSON Patch diffs"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Clients need compact RFC 6902 patches for successive JSON documents. A single root `replace` is
+valid but defeats the feature's purpose for a local change. Arrays need deterministic handling that
+recognizes both element edits and insertions or removals.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate both inputs as JSON values and generate deterministic structural patches. Recurse into
+objects by key, escaping every JSON Pointer token; remove absent source keys, recursively compare
+shared keys, and add target-only keys. For arrays, use deterministic sequence alignment: retain
+deeply equal elements, prefer recursively generated changes for aligned elements, and otherwise use
+`add` or `remove` operations at the current index. Clone every value embedded in a generated
+operation so the patch has no mutable references to either input.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Small nested edits produce operations at their actual pointer instead of a root replacement, and
+common array insertions and removals remain compact. The generator has no runtime dependency and
+may use quadratic work for large, substantially different arrays to choose a stable alignment.
