@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+---
+id: task-005-create-rfc-6902-json-patch-diffs
+type: task
+title: "Create RFC 6902 JSON Patch diffs"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Add an exported `createPatch(from, to)` function that creates an RFC 6902 patch transforming one
+JSON document into another without mutating either input. The patch must communicate local changes
+instead of replacing an entire document for a small change.
+
+## Implementation
+
+Implemented `createPatch(from, to)` in `src/index.ts` following approved decision
+`dl-005-generate-deterministic-structural-json-patch-diffs`. It validates JSON inputs, emits
+deterministically ordered object changes, aligns array elements, escapes JSON Pointer tokens, and
+clones operation values. Unchanged subtrees produce no operations, and aligned containers are
+compared recursively so a small edit stays local. Neither input is mutated.
+
+Documented the API, an example, validation and ownership behavior, and the quadratic cost of array
+alignment after trimming equal prefixes and suffixes in `README.md`.
+
+## Verification
+
+All new acceptance criteria were classified as new behavior and tested red-first: the initial
+test run failed because the requested export did not yet exist. Added tests for localized changes,
+equality, root replacement, escaped and special keys, array edits and duplicates, frozen inputs,
+independent patch values, invalid inputs, and deterministic ordering. The deterministic corpus
+round-trips 1,744 document pairs through serialized patches, and a 10,000-element array insertion
+produces just one operation. Additional frozen-array and construction-order tests characterize
+the implemented behavior.
+
+`npm test` passes all 29 tests, including existing regression tests. `git diff --check` passes.
